Subject: [PATCH] netutils/dhcpc: consume PAD as a single octet

RFC 2132 section 3.1 defines option 0 as a single-octet PAD without a
length field. Treating its following octet as a TLV length can skip
otherwise valid options, including the DHCP message type and lease.
Advance by one byte and resume parsing, including consecutive PADs.

This does not change retry, timeout or option value policy. It is a
protocol parser correction, not a claim about a particular radio failure.

diff --git a/netutils/dhcpc/dhcpc.c b/netutils/dhcpc/dhcpc.c
--- a/netutils/dhcpc/dhcpc.c
+++ b/netutils/dhcpc/dhcpc.c
@@ -87,6 +87,7 @@
 #define DHCPNAK                 6
 #define DHCPRELEASE             7
 
+#define DHCP_OPTION_PAD         0
 #define DHCP_OPTION_SUBNET_MASK 1
 #define DHCP_OPTION_ROUTER      3
 #define DHCP_OPTION_DNS_SERVER  6
@@ -348,6 +349,13 @@ static uint8_t dhcpc_parseoptions(FAR struct dhcpc_state *presult,
     {
       switch (*optptr)
         {
+          case DHCP_OPTION_PAD:
+
+            /* PAD has no length or data octets (RFC 2132, section 3.1). */
+
+            optptr++;
+            continue;
+
           case DHCP_OPTION_SUBNET_MASK:
 
             /* Get subnet mask in network order */
